DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Apart from a few notable exceptions, rc scripts must follow this naming
     policy:

     1.   When possible, use the same name as the ddaaeemmoonn it is referring to.
     2.   It must follow ksh(1) variable naming: begin with an alphabetic or
          underscore character, followed by one or more alphanumeric or under‐
          score characters.  Dashes (‘-’) have to be converted to underscores
          (‘_’).

     Every script under _/_e_t_c_/_r_c_._d follows this pattern:

     1.   Define the _d_a_e_m_o_n variable.
     2.   Define service-specific defaults for one or more _d_a_e_m_o_n___* variables
          (optional).
     3.   Source rrcc..ssuubbrr, which defines default shell functions and variable
          values.
     4.   Override the _p_e_x_p variable or any of the rrcc__** functions and set the
          _r_c___b_g or _r_c___r_e_l_o_a_d variables, if needed.
     5.   Define an rrcc__pprree and/or rrcc__ppoosstt function, if needed.
     6.   Call the rrcc__ccmmdd function as “rc_cmd $1”.

     The following shell functions are defined by rrcc..ssuubbrr:

     rrcc__cchheecckk   Search for processes of the service with pgrep(1) using the
                regular expression given in the _p_e_x_p variable.

     rrcc__ccmmdd _a_c_t_i_o_n
                Run the _a_c_t_i_o_n for the current rrcc..dd script, based on the set‐
                tings of various shell variables.  rrcc__ccmmdd is extremely flexi‐
                ble, and allows fully functional rrcc..dd scripts to be imple‐
                mented in a small amount of shell code.  For a given _a_c_t_i_o_n,
                if the rrcc__$${{aaccttiioonn}} function is not defined, then a default
                function is provided by rrcc..ssuubbrr.  In addition actions can be
                disabled by setting the _r_c___$_{_a_c_t_i_o_n_} variable to “NO”.  For
                example, if “rc_reload=NO” is set in the rrcc..dd script, and
                rrcc__ccmmdd is called for the reload action, an error will be
                raised.  Similarly, the special variable _r_c___u_s_e_r_c_h_e_c_k must be
                set to “NO” if the cchheecckk _a_c_t_i_o_n requires root privileges.

                The _a_c_t_i_o_n argument can be ssttaarrtt, ssttoopp, rreellooaadd, rreessttaarrtt, or
                cchheecckk:

                cchheecckk    Call rrcc__cchheecckk.  Return 0 if the daemon is running or
                         1 if it is not.

                ssttaarrtt    Check that the service is running by calling
                         rrcc__cchheecckk.  If it's not running, call rrcc__pprree if it ex‐
                         ists, then rrcc__ssttaarrtt.

                ssttoopp     Check that the service is running by calling
                         rrcc__cchheecckk.  If it is running, call rrcc__ssttoopp and wait up
                         to 30 seconds for the daemon to properly shutdown.
                         If successful, run rrcc__ppoosstt if it exists.

                rreessttaarrtt  Run the _a_c_t_i_o_n argument ssttoopp, then if successful run
                         ssttaarrtt.

                rreellooaadd   Check that the service is running by calling
                         rrcc__cchheecckk.  If it is running, call rrcc__rreellooaadd.

     rrcc__ccoonnffiiggtteesstt
                Check daemon configuration before running ssttaarrtt, rreellooaadd and
                rreessttaarrtt if implemented by the rc.d(8) script.

     rrcc__eexxeecc    Execute argument using su(1) according to _d_a_e_m_o_n___c_l_a_s_s,
                _d_a_e_m_o_n___e_x_e_c_d_i_r, _d_a_e_m_o_n___u_s_e_r, _d_a_e_m_o_n___r_t_a_b_l_e and _d_a_e_m_o_n___l_o_g_g_e_r
                values.

     rrcc__ppoosstt    This function is run after ssttoopp if implemented by the rc.d(8)
                script.

     rrcc__pprree     This function is run before ssttaarrtt if implemented by the
                rc.d(8) script.

     rrcc__rreellooaadd  Send the _r_c___r_e_l_o_a_d___s_i_g_n_a_l using pkill(1) on the regular ex‐
                pression given in the _p_e_x_p variable.  One has to make sure
                that sending SIGHUP to a daemon will have the desired effect,
                i.e. that it will reload its configuration.

     rrcc__ssttaarrtt   Start the daemon.  Defaults to:

                      rc_exec "${daemon} ${daemon_flags}"

