EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
     rrcc__ccmmdd uses the following shell variables to control its behaviour.

     _d_a_e_m_o_n          The path to the daemon, optionally followed by one or
                     more whitespace separated arguments.  Arguments included
                     here are always used, even if _d_a_e_m_o_n___f_l_a_g_s is empty.
                     This variable is required.  It is an error to source
                     rrcc..ssuubbrr without defining _d_a_e_m_o_n first.

     _d_a_e_m_o_n___c_l_a_s_s    Login class to run the daemon with, using su(1).  This is
                     a read only variable that gets set by rrcc..ssuubbrr itself.  It
                     searches login.conf(5) for a login class that has the
                     same name as the rrcc..dd script itself and uses that.  If no
                     such login class exists then “daemon” will be used.

     _d_a_e_m_o_n___e_x_e_c_d_i_r  Change to this directory before running rrcc__eexxeecc.

     _d_a_e_m_o_n___f_l_a_g_s    Arguments to call the daemon with.

     _d_a_e_m_o_n___l_o_g_g_e_r   Redirect standard output and error to logger(1) using the
                     configured priority (e.g. "daemon.info").

     _d_a_e_m_o_n___r_t_a_b_l_e   Routing table to run the daemon under, using route(8).

     _d_a_e_m_o_n___t_i_m_e_o_u_t  Maximum time in seconds to wait for the ssttaarrtt, ssttoopp and
                     rreellooaadd actions to return.  This is only guaranteed with
                     the default rrcc__ssttaarrtt, rrcc__ssttoopp and rrcc__rreellooaadd functions.

     _d_a_e_m_o_n___u_s_e_r     User to run the daemon as, using su(1).

     _p_e_x_p            A regular expression to be passed to pgrep(1) in order to
                     find the desired process or to be passed to pkill(1) to
                     stop it.  By default this variable contains the _d_a_e_m_o_n
                     and _d_a_e_m_o_n___f_l_a_g_s variables.  To override the default
                     value, an rrcc..dd script has to redefine this variable _a_f_t_e_r
                     sourcing rrcc..ssuubbrr.

     _r_c___b_g           Can be set to YYEESS in an rrcc..dd script to force starting the
                     daemon in background when using the default rrcc__ssttaarrtt.

     _r_c___r_e_l_o_a_d       Can be set to “NO” in an rrcc..dd script to disable the
                     reload action if the respective daemon does not support
                     reloading its configuration.  _T_h_e _s_a_m_e _i_s _p_o_s_s_i_b_l_e_, _b_u_t
                     _a_l_m_o_s_t _n_e_v_e_r _u_s_e_f_u_l_, _f_o_r _o_t_h_e_r _a_c_t_i_o_n_s_.

     _r_c___r_e_l_o_a_d___s_i_g_n_a_l
                     Signal sent to the daemon process (_p_e_x_p) by the default
